module mowd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.missouri.{ frcp6-missouri }

// The Western District of Missouri's own periods under its Local Civil
// Rules, computed under FRCP 6(a), which governs "any local rule". Rules
// that state no period or limit stay out. Periods that restate an FRCP
// period stay in notes: initial disclosures no later than 14 days after
// the FRCP 26(f) conference (L.R. 26.1(a); FRCP 26(a)(1)(C)), and the 14
// days to appeal a magistrate judge's order or object to a recommendation
// and to respond to objections (L.R. 74.1(a)(2), (b)(2); FRCP 72(a),
// (b)(2)), with the extension of the objection time by up to 21 days for
// excusable neglect or good cause (L.R. 74.1(b)(2)), lit/frcp's. Floors
// and caps that are not deadlines stay in notes: the FRCP 26(f)
// conference not earlier than 30 days before the scheduling order is due
// (L.R. 26.1(a)), a proposed dispositive motion deadline within 30 days
// after the proposed discovery close (L.R. 16.1), more than 180 days of
// proposed discovery needing an explanation (L.R. 26.1), and leave to pay
// an in forma pauperis fee within no fewer than 30 days (L.R. 83.7(c),
// (d)). Periods binding only the court, its officers or a special master
// stay in notes: the receiver's reports every 3 months (L.R. 66.1(c)),
// stated in months; the 90-day public-inspection period and the court
// reporter's redacted transcript within 31 days (L.R. 80.1(a)(1), (4));
// and the attorney discipline periods (L.R. 83.6). The misdemeanor appeal
// (L.R. 74.1(d)) and the Local Criminal Rules are lit/mowd-criminal's.
// The earlier W.D. Mo. outline's FRCP flow belongs to lit/frcp, and its
// decisions (Bell Atlantic Corp. v. Twombly, Ashcroft v. Iqbal, Celotex
// Corp. v. Catrett, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Inc., Johnson v. Dayton
// Elec. Mfg. Co., Braden v. Wal-Mart Stores, Inc. and Torgerson v. City of
// Rochester) are FRCP authority not stated in the Local Rules; they are
// removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// Supporting or opposing suggestions: at most 15 pages unless the court
/// orders otherwise; exhibits, signature blocks, certificates of service
/// and statements of fact do not count, nor the table of contents and
/// table of authorities suggestions over 10 pages must have (L.R. 7.0(d)).
limit suggestions { pages <= 15 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(d)" } cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(d)"
/// Reply suggestions: at most 10 pages (L.R. 7.0(d)(1)(C)).
limit reply-suggestions { pages <= 10 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(d)" } cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(d)"

/// A written motion is filed with its supporting suggestions (L.R.
/// 7.0(c)(1), (2)).
event MotionFiled() paper suggestions
/// A motion for summary judgment is filed (L.R. 7.0(c)(2)).
event SummaryJudgmentMotionFiled() paper suggestions
/// Opposing suggestions are filed (L.R. 7.0(c)(3)).
event OpposingSuggestionsFiled() paper suggestions
/// Information in a filed certificate of interest changes before the time
/// to appeal from final judgment expires (L.R. 7.1(c)).
event InterestInformationChanged()
/// The defendant has notice of a Social Security action (L.R. 9.1(b)).
event SocialSecurityNotice()
/// The certified copy of the administrative record is filed (L.R.
/// 9.1(d)(1)).
event AdministrativeRecordFiled()
/// The plaintiff's brief in a Social Security case is served (L.R.
/// 9.1(d)(2)).
event SocialSecurityBriefServed()
/// The Commissioner's brief is served (L.R. 9.1(d)(3)).
event CommissionerBriefServed()
/// Opposing suggestions to a habeas petition are served (L.R. 9.2(h)).
event HabeasOppositionServed()
/// The court grants leave to amend a pleading (L.R. 15.1(b)).
event LeaveToAmendGranted()
/// The parties hold the FRCP 26(f) conference (L.R. 16.1(b)).
event DiscoveryConferenceHeld()
/// The date designated in the original notice for a deposition (L.R.
/// 30.1).
event DepositionDate()
/// The date of the trial setting (L.R. 47.1(c)).
event TrialSetting()
/// Final judgment is entered under FRCP 58 (L.R. 54.1(a)).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// A bill of costs is filed (L.R. 54.1(a)).
event BillOfCostsFiled()
/// Objections to a bill of costs are filed (L.R. 54.1(a)).
event CostObjectionsFiled()
/// The Court of Appeals issues its mandate (L.R. 54.1(b)).
event MandateIssued()
/// A motion for entry of default is filed (L.R. 55.1(a)).
event DefaultMotionFiled()
/// The court announces a decision whose judgment or order requires
/// settlement as to form (L.R. 58.2).
event DecisionAnnounced()
/// A party receives the prevailing party's draft judgment or order (L.R.
/// 58.2).
event DraftJudgmentReceived()
/// A receiver or similar officer takes possession of the estate (L.R.
/// 66.1(b)).
event ReceiverPossession()
/// A verdict is rendered or a judgment entered (L.R. 79.2(a)).
event VerdictOrJudgment()
/// A transcript is filed (L.R. 80.1(a)).
event TranscriptFiled()
/// An attorney not a member of the court's bar enters a limited initial
/// appearance (L.R. 83.5(f)(2)).
event LimitedAppearanceEntered()
/// A party is notified of a filing fee imposed on a person who sought
/// leave to proceed in forma pauperis (L.R. 83.7(e)).
event IfpFeeNotified()

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c)(2): within 14 days after a motion is filed, each
/// party opposing it files opposing suggestions.
deadline opposing-suggestions-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c)(2): for a summary judgment motion a party instead
/// has 21 days to file its opposing suggestions.
deadline summary-judgment-opposition-period: 21.days after SummaryJudgmentMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c)(3): within 14 days after the opposing suggestions
/// are filed, the moving party may file reply suggestions.
deadline reply-suggestions-period: 14.days after OpposingSuggestionsFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.1(c): if the information in a certificate of interest
/// changes before the time to appeal from final judgment expires, the
/// party files an amended certificate within 7 days after the change.
deadline amended-certificate-period: 7.days after InterestInformationChanged() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.1(b): within 90 days after notice of a Social Security
/// action, the defendant serves an answer, which may be limited to a
/// certified copy of the administrative record.
deadline social-security-answer-period: 90.days after SocialSecurityNotice() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.1(d)(1): the plaintiff files and serves its brief within
/// 40 days after the certified copy of the administrative record is filed.
deadline social-security-brief-period: 40.days after AdministrativeRecordFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.1(d)(2): the Commissioner files a brief and serves it
/// within 40 days after service of the plaintiff's brief.
deadline commissioner-brief-period: 40.days after SocialSecurityBriefServed() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.1(d)(3): the plaintiff may file and serve a reply brief
/// within 21 days after service of the Commissioner's brief.
deadline social-security-reply-period: 21.days after CommissionerBriefServed() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.2(h): unless the court extends it, the petitioner files
/// any reply suggestions within 14 days after the respondent's opposing
/// suggestions are served; absent a timely reply and good cause, the court
/// deems admitted all facts well pleaded in the opposing suggestions.
deadline habeas-reply-period: 14.days after HabeasOppositionServed() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 9.2(h)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 15.1(b): when the court grants leave to amend, the moving
/// party files and serves the pleading within 7 days after the grant, or as
/// the court directs.
deadline amended-pleading-period: 7.days after LeaveToAmendGranted() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 15.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 16.1(b): the parties file a proposed scheduling order
/// within 14 days after holding the FRCP 26(f) conference.
deadline proposed-scheduling-order-period: 14.days after DiscoveryConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 16.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 30.1: a party other than the one conducting a deposition
/// that will record it by non-stenographic means files the method and the
/// technician's name, address and employer no later than 3 days before the
/// date designated in the original notice.
deadline recording-notice-period: 3.days before DepositionDate() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 30.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 47.1(c): a party wanting additional peremptory challenges
/// files a motion at least 30 days before the date of the trial setting; a
/// late motion waives the request.
deadline peremptory-challenge-motion-period: 30.days before TrialSetting() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 47.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 54.1(a)(1): a party seeking costs files a verified bill of
/// costs no later than 21 days after entry of final judgment under FRCP
/// 58.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 21.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 54.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 54.1(a)(1): within 14 days after the bill of costs is
/// filed, each objecting party files suggestions stating specific
/// objections; absent a timely objection the Clerk taxes costs as claimed
/// (L.R. 54.1(a)(2)).
deadline cost-objection-period: 14.days after BillOfCostsFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 54.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 54.1(a)(1): within 14 days after objections are filed,
/// the party seeking costs may file reply suggestions.
deadline cost-reply-period: 14.days after CostObjectionsFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 54.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 54.1(b): the Clerk taxes FRAP 39(e) costs if a bill of
/// costs or amended bill is filed within 21 days after the Court of
/// Appeals issues the mandate.
deadline appeal-costs-period: 21.days after MandateIssued() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 54.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 55.1(a)(1): written notice of the intention to move for
/// entry of default is given at least 14 days before the motion is filed.
deadline default-notice-period: 14.days before DefaultMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 55.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 58.2: when the court so orders, the prevailing party
/// prepares, serves and files a draft of the judgment or order within 7
/// days after the decision is announced.
deadline draft-judgment-period: 7.days after DecisionAnnounced() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 58.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 58.2: within 7 days after receiving the draft, any party
/// may file a statement of approval or disapproval of its form, with its
/// objections and a substitute draft if it disapproves.
deadline draft-judgment-response-period: 7.days after DraftJudgmentReceived() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 58.2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 66.1(b): unless the court orders otherwise, a receiver or
/// similar officer files the inventories of the estate as soon as
/// practicable, but not later than 30 days after taking possession.
deadline receiver-inventory-period: 30.days after ReceiverPossession() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 66.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 79.2(a): after trial or as soon as possible, but no more
/// than 14 days after a verdict is rendered or a judgment entered, the
/// offering attorney withdraws any exhibits in the Clerk's custody and
/// gives the Clerk a receipt.
deadline exhibit-withdrawal-period: 14.days after VerdictOrJudgment() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 79.2(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 80.1(a)(2): within 7 days after a transcript is filed,
/// each party wishing to redact personal data identifiers under FRCP 5.2
/// files a Notice of Intent to Redact.
deadline redaction-notice-period: 7.days after TranscriptFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 80.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 80.1(a)(3): within 21 days after the transcript is filed,
/// a party that filed a Notice of Intent to Redact files a statement of
/// the page and line numbers of the identifiers.
deadline redaction-statement-period: 21.days after TranscriptFiled() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 80.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 83.5(f)(2): an attorney not a member of the court's bar
/// who enters a limited initial appearance complies with L.R. 83.5(f)(3)
/// within 14 days after entering it, or may be removed from the case.
deadline admission-compliance-period: 14.days after LimitedAppearanceEntered() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 83.5(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 83.7(e): any party may file written objections to a fee
/// imposed on a person who sought leave to proceed in forma pauperis
/// within 21 days after being notified of the fee.
deadline ifp-fee-objection-period: 21.days after IfpFeeNotified() counted_by frcp6-missouri cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 83.7(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}
